{"step_index":1498,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T14:41:18Z","input_tokens":2090,"cache_read_tokens":158510,"output_tokens":1654,"content":"# Phase 4 Implementation Report — Add Interactive Learning\n\nPhase 4 (**Add Interactive Learning**) has been implemented and verified. Learners can now predict variable values, condition outcomes, and record updates before steps execute, receiving instant feedback and beginner-friendly explanations while preserving all existing execution values, teaching substeps, and navigation controls.\n\n---\n\n### Summary of Changed Files & Rationale\n\n| File | What Was Changed & Why |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| [app_build/index.html](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html) | Added `#btnToggleQuiz` (`🎯 Predict: OFF / ON`) in the top navigation bar, and injected `#interactivePredictCard` directly into Area 2 under the active code box. |\n| [app_build/styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css) | Added styling for `#btnToggleQuiz.active` (warm amber glow), `.interactive-predict-card` container, badge groups, prominent question typography, interactive choice buttons (`.predict-choice-btn` with hover, `:disabled`, `.is-correct`, `.is-incorrect`), feedback explanation box (`.predict-result-box`), and responsive single-column layouts on mobile screens. |\n| [app_build/explainer.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/explainer.js) | Implemented `buildPredictQuestion(step, prevStep, nextStep)` within `RuleBasedExplainer`, generating interactive prediction challenges for additions (`c += nums[i]`), record checks (`c >= ans`), negative resets (`c < 0`, `c = 0`), and general comparisons without fabricating runtime values or calling external APIs. |\n| [app_build/app.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js) | Initialized `this.predictModeEnabled` (default: `false`) and `this.stepAnswers` (cache map); wired `#btnToggleQuiz` and `#btnSkipPredict`; implemented `renderInteractivePredictCard(step, currentSubstep)` to evaluate answers, reveal feedback\n<truncated 1950 bytes>\n**Auto Play** automatically pauses on encountering an unanswered prediction question, allowing the learner to answer at their own pace without being skipped.\n   - Moving between substeps preserves the prediction card smoothly.\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Test Results\n\nA test suite ([scratch/test_phase4.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_phase4.js)) was executed using Node.js:\n\n- **Syntax Check**: `node -c app_build/explainer.js`, `app_build/app.js`, and `app_build/engine.js` passed with zero errors.\n- **HTML & CSS Elements**: All required selectors (`#btnToggleQuiz`, `#interactivePredictCard`, `.predict-choice-btn.is-correct`, `.predict-result-box`) verified present.\n- **Execution Output Integrity Across All 5 Test Inputs**:\n  - `Mixed [-2, 1, -3, 4, -1, 2, 1, -5, 4]` $\\rightarrow$ Final Output: `6` (29 questions generated)\n  - `All-Negative [-5, -2, -8, -1, -4]` $\\rightarrow$ Final Output: `-1` (20 questions generated)\n  - `All-Positive [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]` $\\rightarrow$ Final Output: `15` (15 questions generated)\n  - `Single Negative [-7]` $\\rightarrow$ Final Output: `-7` (4 questions generated)\n  - `Single Positive [42]` $\\rightarrow$ Final Output: `42` (3 questions generated)\n- **Question Structure Validation**: 100% of generated questions contain non-empty prompts, at least 2 choices, valid `correctIndex` within bounds, matching `correctValue`, and educational explanations.\n- **State Preservation**: Backward and forward step navigation correctly restores previous answers and reveal modes.\n- **Total Tests Passed**: **44 / 44 tests (100% success rate)**.\n\n---\n\n### Remaining Limitations Before Phase 5\n\n1. Prediction questions are currently triggered for single-step arithmetic, comparisons, and resets; compound expressions involving custom user-defined multi-argument functions display the general True/False prediction rather than intermediate function returns.\n2. An optional question score counter (e.g. `3/5 Correct`) is not yet displayed in the top bar.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
